error[ffi_parameter_type]: `p` of `pt_peek_any` lends a whole record to C, and the header takes it as `const void *` — C converts any record's address to that in silence, and how far it reaches is another argument this declaration ties to nothing
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-a-record-lent-read-only-to-a-header-that-may-write-it.hero:18:26
     |
  18 |     function pt_peek_any(p: Pt lent) -> i64  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |                          ^
  note: §4.19: a record lent read-only crosses as a pointer to `const` of its own struct, and a `void *` drops both the struct and the `const`: write a header of your own that declares a `static inline` function taking `p` as that pointer and handing it on to `pt_peek_any`, and bind that one; or, where C may write it, take it `@p: <record> counted_by <count>`

